From: Trijal Saha <97483939+Trijal08@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 6 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] samsung-sit: send the boot queries stock sends, as often as
 stock sends them

Diffing the AP->CP stream per message id against stock, bounded at the IMS
context request, most of the remaining gap was put there by r61. That
revision collapsed 246 replayed rows to 48 and dropped fourteen getters on
the grounds that a getter cannot configure anything. True, and the wrong
call: stock sends every one of them, and the collapse also cut counts stock
repeats.

Restored, with the counts stock uses -- each identical in all three boot
captures:

    0x0400 GET_IMSI              1 / 1
    0x0403 GET_DEV_ID            1 / 1
    0x070c GET_CELL_INFO_LIST    1 / 1
    0x0711 GET_PS_SERVICE        1 / 1
    0x0718 GET_RADIO_CAPABILITY  4 / 4
    0x0810 GET_STACK_STATUS      1 / 1
    0x091b GET_VOICE_OPERATION   1 / 1
    0x0957 GET_DEVICE_SERVICE    1 / 1
    0x0c01 LPP_SUPL_REQ_ECID     2 / 2
    0x0615 (in no name table)    2 / 0   -- we never sent it at all

and counts raised on entries already present: 0x074f 1->3, 0x0755 1->2,
0x0760 1->2, 0x0762 1->4, 0x0954 1->3 on stack 0 and 1->2 on stack 1.

Only counts that are the same in all three captures are stated. 0x0106,
0x0107, 0x0703, 0x0943, 0x0944, 0x0c20, 0x0c33, 0x0d17, 0x0d3a, 0x0d3b,
0x0d3c, 0x0108 and 0x0740 vary between them -- 0x0703 is 10, 17 and 12 on
one stack -- so they have no single right answer, and pinning one capture's
number is exactly how the replay table this replaced went stale. They are
left where they are and the header records why.

A test pins the stable set, so a number copied from a single boot cannot
slip back in, and the primary-only count goes to four for 0x0615.

